SUMMARY:Monet\, Matisse\, Van Gogh & More: Impressionism at the AGO
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Saturday\, August 29th**\, join me at
  the **Art Gallery of Ontario (AGO) to see the Newest Exhibit that opened 
 this past weekend - Monet\, Matisse\, Van Gogh & More: Impressionism.** Ma
 king its Canadian debut at the AGO\, this sweeping overview of Impressioni
 sm is drawn from the Dallas Museum of Art (DMA)’s exceptional permanent 
 collection. The exhibition includes remarkable works by Monet\, Renoir\, G
 ustave Caillebotte\, Henri Matisse\, Edgar Degas\, Berthe Morisot\, Vincen
 t van Gogh\, Paul Gauguin\, Piet Mondrian\, Edvard Munch\, and more. Arran
 ged in five chronological and thematic sections\, the 50 works on view hig
 hlight how the techniques and subjects of these experimental artists set a
  new course for modern art in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. **Pu
 rchase your ticket for the AGO on Saturday August 29th.**\n\nThe names Cla
 ude Monet\, Berthe Morisot\, and Pierre-Auguste Renoir are among the most 
 recognizable in art history. For over a century\, these originators of Imp
 ressionism have often been celebrated for defining modern art\; but in the
  early days of their careers\, they were considered controversial. Using e
 xperimental techniques to depict landscapes\, public life\, still lifes an
 d interiors\, they ushered in a new wave of avant-garde painting\, profoun
 dly inspiring the next generation. On view now on Level 4 of the AGO\, *Th
 e Impressionist Revolution: Monet to Matisse from the Dallas Museum of Art
 * illustrates the inception and ripple effects of a beloved art movement o
 ver time.\n\nWhile at the AGO\, there are many other exhibits to explore.\
 n\n* [Edna Taçon: Verve and Decorum](https://ago.ca/exhibitions/edna-taco
 n-verve-and-decorum) until Aug 30\n* [Painted Presence: Rembrandt and his 
 Peers](https://ago.ca/exhibitions/painted-presence-rembrandt-and-his-peers
 ) until Oct 4\n* [Yayoi Kusama's INFINITY MIRRORED ROOM - LET'S SURVIVE FO
 REVER](https://ago.ca/exhibitions/yayoi-kusamas-infinity-mirrored-room-let
 s-survive-forever) until Oct 25\n* [Ranbir Sidhu: No Limits](https://ago.c
 a/exhibitions/ranbir-sidhu-no-limits) until Jan 3/27\n* [The J.S. McLean C
 entre for Indigenous & Canadian Art](https://ago.ca/exhibitions/j.s.-mclea
 n-centre-indigenous-canadian-art-2021)\n* [Kazuo Nakamura: Blue Dimension]
 (https://ago.ca/exhibitions/kazuo-nakamura-blue-dimension)\n* [Remade: Cla
 y\, Plaster\, Stone](https://ago.ca/exhibitions/remade-clay-plaster-stone)
 \n* [Bill Nasogaluak](https://ago.ca/exhibitions/bill-nasogaluak)\n* And M
 ore\n\n**COST**\nAdult: $30 + service fee. Option to purchase an Annual pa
 ss for $40 total (no service fee)\, and visit as many times as you want ov
 er a period of one year.\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n**Ticket Policy**:
  All sales are final\, no refunds or exchanges.\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **R
 SVP Yes** **\\- everyone goes on the waitlist until they post they purchas
 ed their ticket**\n* **[Purchase](https://visit.ago.ca/59813/60285)** **yo
 ur own ticket by selecting Saturday August 29th\,** post you have your tic
 ket and I will move you to going.\n\nA reminder will be sent the day befor
 e with my cell and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSVPs close
  1 day prior and the Waitlist will be removed at that time. Cancellations 
 will result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\
 n**Meet me at: 3pm to the left side of the ticket scanner\, inside the ent
 rance of the AGO at 317 Dundas St. W. We will then head directly together 
 to the 4th floor for The Impressionism Exhibit.**\n\nAttendees can wonder 
 around to see which Exhibits they like\, and also visit the Store.\n\n**Me
 et me at 5:30pm: just inside the entrance doors to head out for dinner nea
 rby**\n\nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after.
